.md
In this particular case, the sample was mounted at a small angle relative to the laboratory coordinate system. Because the mirrors rotate the polarization, the eigenvectors also exhibit slight ellipticity. We can inspect these vectors directly:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
In this particular case, the sample was mounted at a small angle relative to the laboratory coordinate system. Because the mirrors rotate the polarization, the eigenvectors also exhibit slight ellipticity. We can inspect these vectors directly:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
OpticalAxisAnalysis[d[Quantity[1.25, "Terahertz"]]];
%[["Eigenpolarizations", All, {"JonesVector", "AzimuthDeg"}]] // TableView 

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef["F19f09a28-0a21-4427-9484-a20231c0437c"])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgUJG1qmGVgmGlnoGiQaGeqamBiZ61qaWJjoJhoZGBkbJhuYGJsnAwCFpRS5"*)(*]VB*)

